{"tool_name":"cbgt","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"CBGT","home":"https://github.com/CoAxLab/CBGT","license":"Other","summary":"Spiking Neural Network of cortico-basal ganglia-thalamus (CBGT) pathways.","addition_date":"2019-08-09T13:21:39Z","last_update_date":"2020-06-16T10:55:25Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:CBGT","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"jonrubin@pitt.edu","name":"Jonathan Rubin","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1513-1551","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"timothyv@andrew.cmu.edu","name":"Timothy Verstynen","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4720-0336","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/CoAxLab/CBGT/blob/master/README.md"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"maturity":"Mature","name":"CBGT","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"hans","publication":[{"doi":"10.1371/JOURNAL.PCBI.1006998","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2019 Dunovan et al.Cortico-basal-ganglia-thalamic (CBGT) networks are critical for adaptive decision-making, yet how changes to circuit-level properties impact cognitive algorithms remains unclear. Here we explore how dopaminergic plasticity at corticostriatal synapses alters competition between striatal pathways, impacting the evidence accumulation process during decision-making. Spike-timing dependent plasticity simulations showed that dopaminergic feedback based on rewards modified the ratio of direct and indirect corticostriatal weights within opposing action channels. Using the learned weight ratios in a full spiking CBGT network model, we simulated neural dynamics and decision outcomes in a reward-driven decision task and fit them with a drift diffusion model. Fits revealed that the rate of evidence accumulation varied with inter-channel differences in direct pathway activity while boundary height varied with overall indirect pathway activity. This multi-level modeling approach demonstrates how complementary learning and decision computations can emerge from corticostriatal plasticity.","authors":[{"name":"Clapp M."},{"name":"Dunovan K."},{"name":"Rubin J."},{"name":"Verstynen T."},{"name":"Vich C."}],"citationCount":8,"date":"2019-05-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"PLoS Computational Biology","title":"Reward-driven changes in striatal pathway competition shape evidence evaluation in decision-making"},"pmcid":"PMC6534331","pmid":"31060045","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Machine learning","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3474"},{"term":"Molecular interactions, pathways and networks","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0602"},{"term":"Transcription factors and regulatory sites","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0749"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"CBGT","home":"https://bio.tools/CBGT","license":"Other","summary":"Spiking Neural Network of cortico-basal ganglia-thalamus (CBGT) pathways.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:cbgt/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":false,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true},"license":{"open_source":false,"osi":false},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":21,"citations":[{"count":2,"year":"2021"},{"count":2,"year":"2023"},{"count":2,"year":"2026"},{"count":3,"year":"2022"},{"count":3,"year":"2024"},{"count":4,"year":"2020"},{"count":5,"year":"2025"}],"doi":"10.1371/journal.pcbi.1006998","pmcid":"PMC6534331","pmid":"31060045","ref_count":75,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"1